  <prompt>
    Activate the embedded Compose "Draft Alternative" tool for user-driven per-section rewrites: resolve the
    compose-draft-alternative bindingId:'' stub to the real binding, and ensure the execution-trace flow works so
    the user can select a flagged section and generate a standards-based alternative. Redlines are user-driven per
    section — NOT AI batch-applied.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    SPAARKE Compose client developer. Expert in ComposeAiToolbar, the single-edit compose-draft-alternative action,
    and the execution-trace flow.
  </role>

  <goal>
    Selecting a flagged clause and invoking "Draft Alternative" runs compose-draft-alternative (bound, not stubbed)
    and returns a standards-based rewrite the user can apply per section; the execution trace surfaces.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      compose-draft-alternative is a built single-edit rewrite tool wired in ComposeAiToolbar.tsx (~:324) but with
      bindingId:''. The user flow (north star): go to each highlighted section → select → Draft Alternative using
      firm standards → apply → save. Redlines are user-driven, comments-first — the batch synthesizer concern is moot.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/ (ComposeAiToolbar.tsx)</file>
      <file>infra/dataverse/actions/compose-draft-alternative.action.json</file>
      <file>infra/dataverse/sprk_playbookconsumer-rows.json</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>022 (bindings seeded; the draft-alternative binding GUID resolvable).</dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-039">Draft Alternative is a single-edit action in the closed catalog; bind it to the real binding GUID (no empty bindingId).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Rewrites are user-invoked per section; the tool does NOT auto-apply across the document. The alternative uses firm standards (the seeded standard / draft-alternative Action's grounding).</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
