  <notes>
    Closes the review→revise loop. Keep it user-driven per section per the confirmed flow.

    COMPLETION FINDING (2026-07-26): investigation found the entire bindingId-resolution +
    trace-surfacing mechanism this task asks for was ALREADY SHIPPED by the prior merged
    `spaarkeai-compose-r2`/`compose-r4` projects (tasks 042/047/048/064) — before this
    project's task 022 dependency even landed. No production file needed a change.
    Verified (not assumed):
      - `useComposeToolbarActivation` (useComposeToolbarActivation.ts) fetches
        `GET /api/ai/capabilities?surface=compose` and calls
        `registerComposeAiToolbarAction({...match, bindingId})` for any returned capability
        whose `consumerType` matches a DEFAULT_ACTIONS `id` — this is the IDENTICAL
        capability-discovery, no-hardcoded-GUID mechanism task 022 used
        (`useCapabilityDiscovery`), just the compose-package-local sibling of it. It is
        already wired into BOTH known Compose mount hosts: `ComposeDirectWidget.tsx`
        (SpaarkeAi direct-widget door, used by the NDA `mountFileInCompose` open path) and
        `composeEditor.registration.ts` (LegalWorkspace layout-door). `ComposeAiToolbar.tsx`'s
        `bindingId: ''` in `DEFAULT_ACTIONS` is BY DESIGN (the file's own "PHASE-4 STUB
        BOUNDARY" doc) — the registry overwrite is the resolution mechanism, so hardcoding a
        GUID there would be a regression, not a fix.
      - The Binding row (`consumerType: "compose-draft-alternative"`, disposition
        100000006/compose, `surfaces: "workspace,compose"`, non-empty `toolDescription`) is
        NOT missing — already present in `infra/dataverse/sprk_playbookconsumer-rows.json`,
        exported from the LIVE `spaarkedev1` environment (`$exported: 2026-07-07`). It passes
        `ListTextProjectableBindingsAsync`'s toolDescription filter and the surface filter, so
        `GET /api/ai/capabilities?surface=compose` returns it and the activation hook
        registers it automatically.
      - Execution trace: `ContextPaneController` auto-opens Execution Trace
        (`ComposeTraceHost` → `ExecutionTraceWidget`, ADR-040 ledger-backed) whenever ANY
        Compose tab becomes active (`widgetType==='compose'` OR `layoutName==='Compose'`) —
        not gated to a specific action, so it surfaces for any rewrite dispatched from an
        already-open Compose tab. Covered by
        `ContextPaneController.compose-trace-autoopen.test.tsx` (4 tests, passing).
      - Per-section, not batch: `compose-draft-alternative` is `materializesInEditor: true`
        (DEF-09) — one clause selection → one `target_text`/`new_text` structured edit →
        one pending track-change the user accepts/rejects; it dispatches to the editor's
        DOCUMENT session (not the chat session) so the redline-materialize read coincides
        with the write. Forcing-tested end-to-end in
        `ConversationPane.compose-draft-alternative-session-routing.e2e.test.tsx` (2 tests,
        passing, REAL dispatch + session-keyed ledger, not mocked away).
    Verification run this task: `tsc --noEmit` (Spaarke.Compose.Components) clean;
    `useComposeToolbarActivation.test.tsx` + `ComposeAiToolbar.test.tsx` +
    `ComposeWorkspace.redline-from-ledger.test.tsx` = 28/28 passing;
    `ConversationPane.compose-draft-alternative-session-routing.e2e.test.tsx` +
    `ContextPaneController.compose-trace-autoopen.test.tsx` + `ComposeTraceHost.reachable.test.tsx`
    = 10/10 passing. Full detail: `projects/ai-advanced-capabilities-nda-r1/notes/task-033-draft-alternative-trace-activation.md`.
    Manual live UI verification (select clause → Draft Alternative → rewrite → apply, in a
    deployed NDA-REVIEW org) is env-blocked in this session (no live org/credentials) — not
    faked, per task instruction.
  </notes>

